From 37af85da90bc0f0f22387bce812a0c73da2b9776 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:45:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 222/270] build: no i2c_hid in the Haiku package on 32-bit ARM

i2c_hid only finds its devices through ACPI, which 32-bit ARM does not
have. There the kernel tried to load it, and failed on the missing ACPI
bus manager, every time the input drivers were scanned: 183 times in
the syslog of one boot.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
---
 build/jam/packages/Haiku | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/jam/packages/Haiku b/build/jam/packages/Haiku
index 535d1030dd..b44b05ef78 100644
--- a/build/jam/packages/Haiku
+++ b/build/jam/packages/Haiku
@@ -150,7 +150,7 @@ AddNewDriversToPackage network :
 AddNewDriversToPackage input :
 	hyperv_hid@x86,x86_64
 	i2c_elan
-	i2c_hid
+	i2c_hid@!arm
 	virtio_input
 	;
 AddNewDriversToPackage display :
